WEBVTT

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:07.750
Stepping out on
an ordinary Sunday

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:14.260
Stepping out!
A miracle's gonna happen

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:16.090
It's my day!

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.670
Maybe I'll throw off my pajamas

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:34.080
and head out to see her right now

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:41.450
I always turned my eyes away,
thinking she'd hate me

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:48.860
Now I'm saying goodbye
to that negative attitude

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:54.630
My favorite shoes
will always take me

00:00:57.130 --> 00:01:01.770
To a place where I'll be happy

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:09.280
It's not someone else
I want to embrace

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:15.420
But a version of
myself that's not fake

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:18.490
I just want to walk

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:22.020
Not on tip-toe

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:26.000
Not downcast, either

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:34.900
Just I'm stepping out
on an ordinary Sunday

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:41.340
Stepping out!
Making a little try, try, try

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.610
It's my day!

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:52.650
I...

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:55.860
Tsukasa asked me
to go out with him.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.930
He said he'd try to learn
to love me.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.870
I didn't realize how much
I'd come to love Tsukasa.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.720
<i>I won't have any regrets...</i>

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:47.740
<i>...or so I thought...</i>

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:53.580
<i>I thought that this would
solve everything.</i>

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:02.390
<i>But there's an ache in my heart...</i>

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:33.990
But...

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:42.990
I guess... this is for the best, right?

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:53.010
"The Dawning of a New Day"

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.370
Good morning!

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:55.510
Good morning!

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.020
Good morning...

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.750
<i>I wonder if Domyoji is coming today.</i>

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:03.810
<i>How should I face him?</i>

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:06.280
<i>This is so depressing...</i>

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:08.550
Tsukushi!

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:12.860
Hey, Tsukushi!

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:17.160
Oh, Makiko! Good morning!

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:20.900
What's wrong? You look down.

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:24.330
Oh, well...

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:28.280
I was up late last night and
I'm kind of out of it.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:34.140
I see. I was surprised because
you looked so depressed.

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:39.760
Depressed? Me? I'm not that fragile.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:42.480
Of course, you're right.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:47.590
<i>That's right.</i>

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:51.530
<i>It's not like me to be depressed
over something like this!</i>

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:54.530
<i>Que sera, sera!</i>

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:56.380
Good morning.

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:57.070
Good morning.

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:00.310
Let's run.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:04.670
Tsukushi! What's going on?!

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:08.980
She was so cute when she cried...

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:12.290
...her shoulders shaking
and her face all scrunched up.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:18.060
I thought Shigeru was easygoing,
so it took me by surprise.

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:19.990
I can't believe it!

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:22.860
Did Tsukasa really ask her
to go out with him?

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:25.570
Could that guy actually say
something like that?

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:27.940
Well, why don't you ask him?

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:35.100
<i>Will you go out with me?</i>

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.120
<i>You betcha! Ook ook!</i>

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:40.740
No! No way! I can't see it.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:43.990
Tsukasa? Saying <i>that?</i> Scary.

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:48.870
Come on...
You should be happy for him.

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:51.820
Your leader's taken another step
toward maturity.

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:56.290
Makino... What's with that attitude?

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:57.940
Aren't you in shock?

00:05:58.460 --> 00:05:58.990
Huh?

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:01.390
Tsukushi!

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:03.610
Kazuya!

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:07.790
I'm so sorry, my class ran long.

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:09.640
I brought my lunch.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:12.400
Ta-da!

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:16.180
Wow! Your lunch looks delicious!

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:18.180
This burdock and beef roll...

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:21.410
Your mom made this for us
when we were in elementary school.

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:25.180
She gave me a portion for you, too.

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:26.520
Really?

00:06:26.850 --> 00:06:28.630
Let's share our lunches, then.

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:31.590
A picnic?

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:35.560
Burdock and beef rolls...?
What's that?

00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:37.100
Here!

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:41.300
Would you two like to try some?
Bet you've never tried this.

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:46.470
This rolled egg is my specialty.
This is what commoners eat.

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:52.860
Delicious!

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:54.310
Isn't it?

00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:58.280
If you eat that, you'll get sick.

00:07:00.950 --> 00:07:01.430
Tsukasa...

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:06.720
I've looked all over,
and I find you two here...

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:10.290
Food like this is best
for your health.

00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:13.340
Rich foods can cause disease
later in life.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:16.870
Can it, will you?
You sound like an old fart.

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:18.250
Oh, yeah...

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:19.790
Domyoji...

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:20.440
What?

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:24.090
Everybody's talking about it.
Is it true you've got a girlfriend?

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:30.230
Yeah.

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:32.580
F-for real?

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:37.250
Really? So it's true!
You've finally given Tsukushi up!

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:40.810
Ouch! What's the deal?!

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:43.070
That's great!

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:48.480
Congratulations.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:51.480
I don't want your congratulations.

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:57.440
So, after 18 years,
Tsukasa finally has a girl.

00:07:58.140 --> 00:07:59.540
He's finally an average Joe.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.980
I'll miss the old Tsukasa.

00:08:02.510 --> 00:08:03.380
Shut up.

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:10.590
<i>The instant I said "Congratulations,"
something ended.</i>

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:28.160
<i>All the times he kissed me...</i>

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:45.780
<i>...and embraced me...</i>

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:02.660
<i>All of that is over...</i>

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:07.390
Before you know it, the clematis
has wilted and died...

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:09.230
Ms. Urara...

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:19.510
But in death,
it gains a new freedom.

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:35.390
And... it can leave this hill
to bloom somewhere else.

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:41.130
<i>Freedom...</i>

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:48.000
But... Maybe it loves this hill.

00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:52.480
It doesn't really want to leave,
it just has to.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:55.480
Yes...

00:10:56.110 --> 00:10:58.380
A flower can't choose its own fate.

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:02.080
<i>It can't choose its fate?</i>

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:25.840
<i>My wish was... to be free of Domyoji.</i>

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:28.680
<i>And now...</i>

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:37.420
<i>Now...</i>

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:40.490
<i>It's about to begin...</i>

00:11:41.060 --> 00:11:44.860
<i>A new day...</i>

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:19.190
Tsukasa... Wait up!

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:25.160
Why do you walk so fast?
This isn't a race!

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:26.620
Slow down, will you?!

00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:31.000
Shut up, will you?
I hate walking slow!

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:36.940
This isn't a date!

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:39.570
This is no different
than before!

00:12:40.180 --> 00:12:42.580
I was looking forward to this so much...

00:12:43.420 --> 00:12:47.720
You haven't said anything to me.
You haven't even looked at me!

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:53.090
I don't know why we're even
walking together!

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:14.710
Okay... What should I do?

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:20.450
First, come next to me.

00:13:26.690 --> 00:13:27.790
Come on!

00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:46.840
Talk like you're enjoying yourself,
and match your stride to mine.

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:48.280
What a pain in the ass.

00:13:49.650 --> 00:13:52.110
What d'you think you're doing?
Let go of my arm!

00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:55.980
Why not?!
You're my boyfriend, after all.

00:13:59.220 --> 00:14:00.890
I was so happy...

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:03.130
when you said you'd learn
to love me.

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:06.860
I can believe it, can't I?

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:12.840
Quit it, already...
I said I would, didn't I?

00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:15.070
When?

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:16.070
Who knows?

00:14:17.270 --> 00:14:18.140
Eventually.

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:31.990
So... Are things going well?

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:36.120
Yes. Shigeru is more aggressive
at present...

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:38.760
They seem to be meeting
2-3 times a week.

00:14:40.430 --> 00:14:43.770
I see. Then Tsukasa
has finally come to his senses.

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:47.330
And what about Tsukushi Makino?

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:49.300
Well, er...

00:14:50.100 --> 00:14:53.170
She doesn't seem to be meeting Tsukasa
outside of school, but...

00:14:55.810 --> 00:14:58.480
Good evening! It's me, again!

00:15:00.180 --> 00:15:02.980
She's back again.
What's with that girl?

00:15:03.450 --> 00:15:05.020
Coming in!

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:11.230
Oh, that looks good. I'm so hungry!

00:15:12.330 --> 00:15:13.890
Please help yourself...

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:16.230
We don't have anything much.

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:17.800
Hurray!

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:26.940
Thank you! You always have food
I never ate before.

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:31.210
Delicious!

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:40.890
<i>Is this my "new day"?</i>

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:47.690
<i>Why me? What's with my life?</i>

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:51.760
Are you listening to me, Tsukushi?

00:15:55.030 --> 00:15:55.700
Yeah, sure.

00:15:56.400 --> 00:16:00.000
So, I invited Tsukasa to go to the park.

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:01.910
The park?

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:05.380
Sure. It's usually pretty romantic.

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:08.180
You know... you get your man 
in touch with nature...

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:09.380
Nature?

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:16.280
He didn't even try to kiss me!
Can you believe that?

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:16.850
What?!

00:16:18.690 --> 00:16:21.560
Worse, all he did was sit there
silent as a stone!

00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:23.760
Is that what sweethearts do?!

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:25.260
Well...

00:16:26.930 --> 00:16:30.640
<i>Why do I have to listen to this?</i>

00:16:31.270 --> 00:16:32.040
Tsukushi!

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:34.240
Did you ever kiss Tsukasa?

00:16:38.340 --> 00:16:40.580
So you did!
Oh, how lucky! Lucky you!

00:16:43.280 --> 00:16:44.580
<i>Lucky, how?</i>

00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:50.220
I wonder if he still loves you.

00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:53.480
O-Of course not!

00:16:53.480 --> 00:16:57.460
It's amazing that he's seeing a girl
three times in a week!

00:16:58.630 --> 00:16:59.230
Really?

00:16:59.530 --> 00:17:00.430
Really!

00:17:01.030 --> 00:17:05.210
If his F4 buddies find out he walked
arm-in-arm with you...

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:06.640
...they'll die from shock.

00:17:07.570 --> 00:17:08.380
For sure?

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:09.540
Sure, I'm sure.

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:14.840
I see... You're right...

00:17:15.250 --> 00:17:18.450
I'm sorry, Tsukushi...
I'm just a little impatient.

00:17:20.150 --> 00:17:20.850
<i>Shigeru...</i>

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:24.390
I've been too lucky, so far...

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:28.720
I've always gotten what I wanted.

00:17:29.660 --> 00:17:31.260
So it's a little hard on me.

00:17:32.760 --> 00:17:35.300
<i>She really does love him.</i>

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:43.640
<i>This is not like you, Shigeru!
Come on, smile!</i>

00:17:47.640 --> 00:17:50.080
Let's use this to figure out
where your next date will be.

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:52.950
I'm sure things will go better,
this time.

00:17:53.480 --> 00:17:56.050
You're right! Let's do it!

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:06.730
<i>Why must I do all this?</i>

00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:10.600
<i>Stupid!
How much of a pushover am I?!</i>

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:27.520
Every night, Tsukasa's girlfriend 
comes to your home?

00:18:28.150 --> 00:18:30.380
Yeah... I feel sorry for her.

00:18:32.350 --> 00:18:33.250
What a pain...

00:18:33.590 --> 00:18:34.440
She must be bored.

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:38.960
Why don't you talk to Domyoji
about Shigeru?

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:40.160
No, thanks.

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:43.940
You think he'll listen?

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:48.010
Besides, this isn't something a third party
should get involved in.

00:18:51.170 --> 00:18:52.760
If it happens, it happens.

00:18:52.760 --> 00:18:53.840
If not, it won't.

00:18:54.540 --> 00:18:56.440
There are some things
you can't do anything about.

00:18:57.180 --> 00:19:00.850
Yeah... <i>I know that, but...</i>

00:19:02.520 --> 00:19:05.220
<i>He sounds as cold as ever.</i>

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:10.520
<i>But he really seemed to be
speaking from his heart.</i>

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:14.660
<i>I wonder how things are
with him and Shizuka.</i>

00:19:16.360 --> 00:19:19.530
<i>I guess there's really been
nothing between them...</i>

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:21.400
<i>since he returned from Paris...</i>

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:22.470
Tsukasa!

00:19:27.940 --> 00:19:29.980
What? You shouldn't come here.

00:19:31.010 --> 00:19:32.280
It's Shigeru!

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:35.930
What's she doing at our school?

00:19:35.930 --> 00:19:37.090
That's Shigeru?

00:19:37.550 --> 00:19:38.200
Get out of here.

00:19:38.200 --> 00:19:38.820
No.

00:19:39.250 --> 00:19:40.090
Get out!

00:19:40.090 --> 00:19:40.830
No!

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:42.890
They're supposed to be
sweethearts?

00:19:45.590 --> 00:19:46.660
What do you want?

00:19:47.090 --> 00:19:49.100
If you don't back off,
I'll really get angry.

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:53.860
This is getting really serious.

00:19:53.860 --> 00:19:55.470
Maybe we shouldn't be watching.

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:58.100
Why not?

00:19:58.770 --> 00:19:59.510
Kiss me.

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:01.840
Kiss?

00:20:02.610 --> 00:20:05.650
Prove to me that
you don't love Tsukushi anymore.

00:20:15.090 --> 00:20:15.990
<i>Shigeru?</i>

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:23.630
When you're with me, you're always
thinking about something else.

00:20:24.230 --> 00:20:27.860
It's rude to make me feel 
so insecure.

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:34.770
If she means nothing to you,
you can kiss me, can't you?

00:21:02.500 --> 00:21:03.330
Close your eyes.

00:21:57.500 --> 00:22:04.100
Will I ever make it that far?

00:22:04.100 --> 00:22:08.850
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:22:10.670 --> 00:22:18.320
Some day, the whole world

00:22:18.320 --> 00:22:24.130
will have its eyes on me.

00:22:24.130 --> 00:22:31.880
Yeah, after our graduation ceremony

00:22:31.880 --> 00:22:37.500
we all wrote our dreams on the wall.

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:44.120
A lot of time has passed since then

00:22:44.120 --> 00:22:50.520
but I'm just the same as I was on that day!

00:22:50.520 --> 00:22:57.420
Keep trying your best! 
Wishes can come true!

00:22:57.420 --> 00:23:06.300
Let's keep running down
 the road we believe in!

00:23:07.580 --> 00:23:14.210
Will I ever make it that far?

00:23:14.210 --> 00:23:20.270
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:23:20.810 --> 00:23:27.530
Will I ever make it that far?

00:23:27.530 --> 00:23:30.920
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:23:30.920 --> 00:23:36.790
I already made it this far, after all.

00:23:46.490 --> 00:23:47.590
When did it happen...?

00:23:48.120 --> 00:23:51.360
When did talking with Rui Hanazawa
become so easy?

00:23:52.400 --> 00:23:55.500
It's raining outside...
but it's warm in the cafe.

00:23:56.070 --> 00:23:58.330
And just as I was feeling so happy...

00:23:58.530 --> 00:24:01.270
Domyoji?
What are you two doing here?!

00:24:02.170 --> 00:24:05.110
Hana Yori Dango:
"Surprise! A Double Date!"

00:24:05.840 --> 00:24:07.780
Stay calm... stay calm!
